From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Scott Quarrier <squarrier@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 6 Oct 2026 08:31:25 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] server: capacity refusals answer 429 with Retry-After,
 TF_GLM_CAPACITY_STATUS (MiaAI-Lab recipe patch 0081)

A request refused for capacity (CapacityError) got a bare 503 from the CUDA server's handler, which tells a client
nothing about when to come back, and a 400 on the generic server's generate path. MiaAI-Lab's recipe v1.8 renders
every capacity refusal the same way, with patch 0081-tfcap-capacity-status (by johnwhited): 429 with Retry-After: 5,
so the same client backs off instead of stacking (a deliberate deviation from vLLM, whose 503 lets a load balancer
route elsewhere: a single-instance LAN deployment has no other instance). On the AFD split this is the attention
node's HTTP side; with patch 0082's admission cap (TF_GLM_MAX_QUEUED) it is how a request past the cap is refused.
This ports it behind a switch of this tree's own, off by default:

- server/errors.py: admission_response (the patch's), capacity_status() / capacity_status_on() reading
  TF_GLM_CAPACITY_STATUS (0 or unset: off, 1: on; the GLM engine refuses anything else at start, and a refusal never
  fails on it). Unset, admission_response gives TensorFold v0.6.5's 503 without a header.
- cuda/http.py: _json takes headers; the prepare and non-streamed run sites use admission_response, as the patch, and
  so does the tokenizer route (a third site this tree's handler has, which v0.6.5 renders as 503). A streamed request's
  refusal stays the stream's error event: its 200 is sent before the engine runs, in the recipe too.
- server/http.py (the generic handler): _send_json takes headers; its prepare and tokenizer sites use
  admission_response; the generate path's CapacityError branch, as the patch, answers 400 unset (v0.6.5's).
- engine.py: a startup line when the switch is on, and the check of its value.
- THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md: "Capacity refusals as 429 with Retry-After".

Not changed: the Anthropic route keeps its own rendering (503, overloaded_error); the recipe has no Anthropic route.
CapacityError is no longer named in cuda/http.py, so its import there goes (the patch keeps it, unused).

Unset, every site answers as before, byte for byte.

Tests (CPU): tests/test_cuda_capacity_status.py (17), each with the switch unset and on: the switch's values;
admission_response; the CUDA server's prepare, non-streamed run and tokenizer sites (503 without Retry-After unset,
429 with Retry-After: 5 on, the same error body); other refusals stay 400 without the header; a streamed refusal is
the stream's error event either way; a served reply is unchanged; the generic handler's tokenizer route.

Credit: patch 0081 was written by johnwhited (https://github.com/johnwhited) in
MiaAI-Lab/GLM-5.3-Flash-EXL3-2x-DGX-Sparks-TensorFold pull request #48 (commits 2eaf324, 9d2fd5e), with vLLM v1's
admission check as its reference; MiaAI-Lab applied it as contributed (merge 0cbe026, renumbered in e6bc3e0, v1.8 at
